  "locked": true,
  "problems": [],
  "beats": [
    {
      "id": "B01",
      "duration": 19.775,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B01.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "5d58539f3b12802361c44d66d4949d080c659bef9813c212cc4538fadab654d5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "In November 1284, in the French city of Beauvais, part of the highest stone vaults of the Middle Ages came down.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 8.375
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "They stood more than 45 meters above the floor.",
          "start": 8.775,
          "end": 12.725
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "The choir beneath them, the eastern arm of the cathedral, had been in use for just twelve years.",
          "start": 13.125,
          "end": 19.775
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B02",
      "duration": 13.425,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B02.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "d9e2786eda43fc9d0c288f4fdabb3e253959af8ca4433dff72de65aa51887fb1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "And yet many buildings like it are still standing.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.5
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "At Amiens, begun in 1220, the vault rises more than 42 meters, in a building that is tall, slender and filled with light.",
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 13.425
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B03",
      "duration": 15.275,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B03.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "488c2237e8b8feacc6ec8f298a18ed528cef11f01ed74676e808f2ed99a1c8a8",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "The people who built them worked without modern structural calculations, relying on geometry, craft knowledge and experience.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 8.825
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "So how did they raise stone that high?",
          "start": 9.225,
          "end": 12.0
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "And why, sometimes, did it come down?",
          "start": 12.4,
          "end": 15.275
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B04",
      "duration": 12.175,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B04.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "c663af19a180b8b0fa9727d95588963aee7d4b5149a9b67d714fb9aa10625506",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Start with the stone itself.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.4
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Stone has little or no strength when it is pulled apart.",
          "start": 2.8,
          "end": 6.55
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "So a stone building stands largely by keeping its stones pressed together.",
          "start": 6.95,
          "end": 12.175
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B05",
      "duration": 18.325,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B05.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "103a0bca09e9d8d7c842e6202696de02a135414a5581903d9481c5b6eb1589d2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Now put a heavy stone vault on top of two walls.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.625
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "A vault does not simply press down: it also pushes outward, like a bow being bent.",
          "start": 4.025,
          "end": 10.425
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "That outward push is called thrust, and a document from Amiens shows that builders there were well aware of it.",
          "start": 10.825,
          "end": 18.325
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B06",
      "duration": 22.925,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B06.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "c98dfb7a0dda4e5c09d5a21af23361dc0c4ec9bd13d1f39b4b500e579694885a",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Romanesque builders had several ways of covering a great church.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.6
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "In the barrel-vaulted type shown here, the heavy vault pushes outward along the whole length of the wall, so walls and supports are thick, stiffened by buttresses.",
          "start": 5.0,
          "end": 16.1
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Large openings would weaken the wall that holds the vault, so windows tend to stay small.",
          "start": 16.5,
          "end": 22.925
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B07",
      "duration": 19.625,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B07.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "da23603acbbc51699fd0d8a6faeb9c3e91a59d455e2f7c1e00b9196e41d59192",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Gothic builders rearranged that system of support.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.075
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Instead of spreading the push along a thick wall, they directed it toward particular points, and carried it to supports outside.",
          "start": 4.475,
          "end": 13.05
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Three tools made that possible: the pointed arch, the rib vault, and the flying buttress.",
          "start": 13.45,
          "end": 19.625
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B08",
      "duration": 29.975,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B08.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "210e95dd5cac8629022cd37606dc0dd74d771de1f14609bd15a68164e34a7622",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "A pointed arch is two arcs of a circle that meet at a point.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.325
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Over the same span, it can rise higher than a round arch, and a taller arch can push less to the sides.",
          "start": 4.725,
          "end": 12.1
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "How much less depends on its exact shape, its thickness and the weight it carries.",
          "start": 12.5,
          "end": 18.05
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "In one comparison by MIT engineers, a pointed arch did push less than a round one, but that result belongs to those two arches, not to every arch.",
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 29.975
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B09",
      "duration": 28.525,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B09.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "fe2d6fbbf8cb04f1008e62d8074c62db0c871d11fd5a861c1f57cf9eff117b87",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "In 1675, the scientist Robert Hooke summed up an idea about arches in one line.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 7.125
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "As hangs the flexible line, so but inverted will stand the rigid arch.",
          "start": 7.525,
          "end": 13.075
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Hang a chain with a set of weights, and it takes a shape.",
          "start": 13.475,
          "end": 17.375
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "Turn that shape upside down, and it shows a path the force can follow through an arch carrying the same weights.",
          "start": 17.775,
          "end": 25.025
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "text": "Change the weights, and the shape changes too.",
          "start": 25.425,
          "end": 28.525
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B10",
      "duration": 22.775,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B10.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "8e286bcee52e66d54d791163537af1ca0452f02a86e69e8785600bec20c91149",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "The pointed arch was not a Gothic invention.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.6
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "It already appears in Burgundy, at the rebuilding of the abbey of Cluny around 1088, and Columbia University's Amiens project traces it to Islamic sources.",
          "start": 4.0,
          "end": 15.825
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "At the abbey of Saint-Denis, it was used systematically, together with the other new ideas.",
          "start": 16.225,
          "end": 22.775
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B11",
      "duration": 17.6,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B11.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "eed65a02b11a0420df9af10b8140ccad0bd58327884f6ed033494accdb6001ab",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "It had a subtler advantage too.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.775
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Unlike a round arch, a pointed arch can span sections of different widths, called bays, and still reach the same height at its crown.",
          "start": 3.175,
          "end": 12.55
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "That was a valuable asset for keeping complex vaults regular.",
          "start": 12.95,
          "end": 17.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B12",
      "duration": 18.425,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B12.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "c2e3ff9b370a615795d7ff7eee29c16e82f455ed03c65ee6aab38990f149cc1f",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "The second tool is the rib vault.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.875
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "In the four-part vault shown here, two ribs cross diagonally over each bay of the building.",
          "start": 3.275,
          "end": 9.625
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "In this simplified picture, they direct the vault's load toward four points: the piers, or stone pillars, at its corners.",
          "start": 10.025,
          "end": 18.425
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B13",
      "duration": 20.6,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B13.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "5fa517603bc6016df19e13409cdec9a4db249369d8e8b703e81ef9ac74f83e35",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "How exactly these vaults stand has been debated for centuries.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.725
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Engineers following Jacques Heyman assume that the main ribs bring the forces down, and treat the stone between them as a series of parallel arches.",
          "start": 5.125,
          "end": 15.4
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "So even in that reading, the stone between the ribs carries load.",
          "start": 15.8,
          "end": 20.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B14",
      "duration": 31.325,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B14.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "a20a16ef20294c19a1588a2aa5082b0de39e0302a676db9c023b43de90077ae0",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Ribs were not new either.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.325
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Durham Cathedral in England, begun in 1093, was completely covered by ribbed vaults by the time it was finished in 1133.",
          "start": 2.725,
          "end": 12.875
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Its masons refined them in phases over some forty years, and the historian Roger Stalley argues that the ribs there may owe more to appearance and meaning than to structure.",
          "start": 13.275,
          "end": 25.025
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "Columbia's project traces ribs to Islamic, Roman and Byzantine sources.",
          "start": 25.425,
          "end": 31.325
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B15",
      "duration": 17.65,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B15.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "413c8dd05cae7644aab86e0e0bee1de49621d51fec32c9a9de939abfcf572cf9",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Whatever first inspired them, this kind of vault changes the job of the wall.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.725
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "With the vault's load directed toward the piers, the wall between them was no longer its main support.",
          "start": 6.125,
          "end": 13.225
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "It could be thinned, and opened up with wide windows.",
          "start": 13.625,
          "end": 17.65
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B16",
      "duration": 13.725,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B16.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "ee0f8bfbde88f7eea7728d6c8762a133ba31bdfb820b3b6b3bb385bc7eeb05bc",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "But gathering the thrust does not make it go away.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.65
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Even reduced, that sideways push remains a threat to the stability of the whole building.",
          "start": 4.05,
          "end": 10.3
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "It still has to be contained somewhere.",
          "start": 10.7,
          "end": 13.725
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B17",
      "duration": 20.275,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B17.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "4a4eae916cf3e22ab6deddf30aca7098cf967b1e4dc7ed9af680459d4b1d97fe",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "The answer stands outside the building: the flying buttress.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.275
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "It is a stone arch that picks up the thrust where it leaves the vault, carries it across the aisle roof, and brings it down to a massive pier buttress.",
          "start": 4.675,
          "end": 14.75
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Often a pinnacle on top adds weight, to help stabilize the thrust.",
          "start": 15.15,
          "end": 20.275
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B18",
      "duration": 20.675,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B18.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "d23f181839f838d3740b2f607de19a5f3df61046b2e2d772cbc1c85273920f61",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "One way to picture it comes from Columbia's Amiens project.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.475
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "It is as if the thick outer wall had been cut into segments, and each segment turned 90 degrees.",
          "start": 4.875,
          "end": 12.075
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Those segments become rigid supports, standing out from the building, with exposed arches reaching up to the high vaults.",
          "start": 12.475,
          "end": 20.675
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B19",
      "duration": 30.3,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B19.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "96b159740955da4aadd6ad3047d84b4c0ac023e424ecb8f56d98df0a49adbd73",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "According to France's national library, the first flying buttresses were used to consolidate Romanesque churches that threatened to collapse.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 9.2
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "It also says that the slanting timber props used while building the vaults were, in effect, made permanent in stone.",
          "start": 9.6,
          "end": 17.625
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "At Chartres, flying buttresses were part of the original plans.",
          "start": 18.025,
          "end": 22.825
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "And around the east end of Notre-Dame in Paris, they look almost like a giant external skeleton.",
          "start": 23.225,
          "end": 30.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B20",
      "duration": 11.15,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B20.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "da1367804f35985416d64fbbb37992c87894019328b3fae4614079e13528ff04",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Flying buttresses even help carry rainwater off the roof.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.575
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "But above all, builders learned how to exploit them, and cathedrals grew ever taller.",
          "start": 4.975,
          "end": 11.15
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B21",
      "duration": 22.225,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B21.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "1d00fbf56626c48e91b7639922bfd7b5d31046ab222f622180fd5f08cecad327",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Why go to all this trouble?",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.325
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Part of the answer is light.",
          "start": 2.725,
          "end": 5.075
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "At the abbey church of Saint-Denis, Abbot Suger built a new choir between 1140 and 1144.",
          "start": 5.475,
          "end": 13.425
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "Pointed arches run throughout, every vault is ribbed, and monumental stained glass seems to dissolve the whole structure.",
          "start": 13.825,
          "end": 22.225
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B22",
      "duration": 11.35,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B22.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "f357b27d2bbc599f48d3135d4ac8dc17ae88154aef716d90daf52c2e333c4a1e",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "For Suger, light was a sign, a bridge to the divine.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.25
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "France's national library says the new style had to let in as much light as possible.",
          "start": 4.65,
          "end": 11.35
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B23",
      "duration": 7.625,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B23.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "8775c6f8ae17121ff928a2fe1258ccc74685661b73e8e5de5d53fa5cf84280a3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "At Chartres, some 2,500 square meters of stained glass survive, most of it original.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 7.625
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B24",
      "duration": 17.65,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B24.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "47b5e92a4361870c14aa889338ad42c4d8aab98c2e9284b6a0c104f215dad6e2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "How new was all of this?",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.35
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Some historians call Gothic a revolution in the art of building, while others see a creative step rooted in continuity.",
          "start": 2.75,
          "end": 11.275
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Suger's own crypt still relies almost entirely on round arches and groin vaults.",
          "start": 11.675,
          "end": 17.65
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B25",
      "duration": 16.975,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B25.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "93913c72c0a82beb8cb1f562ea0fb883f64732719f07ac58c17a31a0d3464e6e",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "So how did they do all this, without modern structural calculations?",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.175
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Master builders used geometrical rules, developed through centuries of trial and error.",
          "start": 5.575,
          "end": 12.025
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "They scaled up the same proportions for new, larger elements.",
          "start": 12.425,
          "end": 16.975
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B26",
      "duration": 15.0,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B26.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "30ed56f0b3ba92f6edaea7dba1a2ecc94b503a14e68876362b268f0cd09300eb",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "At Amiens, setting out the site began with ropes pegged to the ground.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.85
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Squares with perfect right angles controlled the plan, and templates for piers, windows and vaults were designed with straight-edge and compass.",
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 15.0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B27",
      "duration": 22.65,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B27.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "b8a9341f33891a6995f3cc42088f5c0b05e3dd49bc2c72fbaaaf0962c8709778",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Arches were usually drawn full size on the ground, then divided into wedge-shaped stones called voussoirs.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 7.55
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Each voussoir was cut to a wooden template, and the stones were laid on a rigid wooden frame called centering.",
          "start": 7.95,
          "end": 15.45
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "The frame came away only once the mortar had set: at Amiens, after a couple of months or so.",
          "start": 15.85,
          "end": 22.65
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B28",
      "duration": 12.85,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B28.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "f82a97f59f5bf17b6bf799ef54a08859e026ff27848f79c1b645132000d62404",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Carpenters built the scaffolding, the formwork for the vaults and the lifting gear.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.45
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "They also tied the upper piers with wood, and later iron, to stop the arches pushing them over.",
          "start": 5.85,
          "end": 12.85
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B29",
      "duration": 10.325,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B29.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "4d72acd1f9c3056cdb727491cb6ca0bd8c47aa419d53f8733564a2a7abeb4977",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "And there was little room for error.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.65
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "The whole stone skeleton relies on lining up the thrust of each arch with the buttress that supports it.",
          "start": 3.05,
          "end": 10.325
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B30",
      "duration": 12.1,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B30.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "802bbf7af47b0b3f0acf2e4690a20bdf66a7de37360b80f4d1acb6083e1ab678",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "All of this took generations of work.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.95
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "The foundation stone of Amiens was laid in 1220, and its main roof was not finished until about 1310.",
          "start": 3.35,
          "end": 12.1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B31",
      "duration": 14.025,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B31.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "c78ba68906ee91dcc022a777257f30c120abb7317edd1e46456cff896a929ede",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Which brings us back to Beauvais.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.6
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "In 1225, a fire damaged the old Romanesque choir, and the bishop decided to rebuild it, inspired by the greatest buildings of his time.",
          "start": 3.0,
          "end": 14.025
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B32",
      "duration": 20.225,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B32.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "06631bd91addee17419cf53557bbee6080dcfba4fa62d8dd93d2e50996e13247",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "By the 1250s, the two lower levels of the new choir were finished.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.125
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Then the bishop apparently decided to go beyond the planned proportions, adding about five meters to the upper windows, and so to the vaults.",
          "start": 5.525,
          "end": 15.275
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "By 1272, the clergy could use the new choir.",
          "start": 15.675,
          "end": 20.225
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B33",
      "duration": 9.6,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B33.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "7de0d2181fb1e28392c1f19ad479420040ba4835d3ea89a489a607d12df02cc7",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Its vault rose more than 45 meters, a few meters above Amiens.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.525
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "These were the highest vaults built in the Middle Ages.",
          "start": 5.925,
          "end": 9.6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B34",
      "duration": 15.475,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B34.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "71e21b89a58a67667583074ab89f64e26e8b2d782fcd31ff42e78d2b1d249671",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Then, in November 1284, part of the vaults over the choir came down.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 5.825
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "The architect Viollet-le-Duc, writing centuries later, called it the last limit that the great churches of the 13th century could reach.",
          "start": 6.225,
          "end": 15.475
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B35",
      "duration": 30.3,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B35.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "b55a66794b3e06ce4ba5f1199793f11bbe42980cd3c1498c1a61a29530e8b292",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Why it happened is still debated.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.675
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Some blame settling masonry that broke the flying buttresses.",
          "start": 3.075,
          "end": 7.775
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Others point to gusts of wind setting the buttress system resonating, or to slow settlement of the foundations.",
          "start": 8.175,
          "end": 16.125
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "A 2024 study found nothing to justify a foundation cause.",
          "start": 16.525,
          "end": 22.2
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "text": "Its authors argue that raising the vaults, against proven proportions, left the upper parts too flexible.",
          "start": 22.6,
          "end": 30.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B36",
      "duration": 18.325,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B36.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "dfbf653761388d6aeba4e9fecd88b0bb8221df4fe003b74fd718513bf1581c4b",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "The repair tells its own story.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.65
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "New piers went up between the old ones, turning three bays into six.",
          "start": 3.05,
          "end": 8.2
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "The work was not finished until 1340: as the historian Stephen Murray put it, it took longer to repair the choir than to build it.",
          "start": 8.6,
          "end": 18.325
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B37",
      "duration": 36.125,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B37.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "c922d2f44e870e55e1bb68f818e8c2c8490e6c8dc6cb334d03da366d5038e2bf",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "In the sixteenth century, work began again, with a new transept, the cross-arm of the building.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 6.45
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Then, instead of a nave, the builders raised a lantern tower and spire about 150 meters high, finished in 1569.",
          "start": 6.85,
          "end": 16.525
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "It rested on four slender piers, and the sources point to a lack of support on the west side, where the nave had not been built.",
          "start": 16.925,
          "end": 26.025
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "In 1573, just four years after it was finished, the tower came down.",
          "start": 26.425,
          "end": 32.525
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "text": "The great Gothic nave was never built.",
          "start": 32.925,
          "end": 36.125
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B38",
      "duration": 20.725,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B38.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "c544477a8e148c20c880dce69bf06c04eb45da8cc1e4c217c77e137599820ac8",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Beauvais was not alone.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.325
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "At Amiens, within two centuries, the piers at the crossing, where the arms of the building meet, were threatening collapse.",
          "start": 2.725,
          "end": 10.65
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Between 1497 and 1500, an iron chain was installed to stop the movement, and it still runs through the building today.",
          "start": 11.05,
          "end": 20.725
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B39",
      "duration": 20.55,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B39.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "5af3cdef3de206f81242b8708ddef323d81f65a2b27f1e42cbf8ba14a33eb7d5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "So why do these buildings stand at all?",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.9
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "One answer from modern engineers is that the stone's strength is rarely the limit.",
          "start": 3.3,
          "end": 9.45
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Stresses in masonry are typically only a fraction of what the stone can bear, and in most cases structures fail through instability, not a lack of strength.",
          "start": 9.85,
          "end": 20.55
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B40",
      "duration": 28.05,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B40.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "ff0c9c78bbca10d2c1384985f31c0ceb257979f926c8b692cfe7cb11db061791",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Picture one idealized arch, and the path of the force through its stones, which engineers call the line of thrust.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 8.275
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "This analysis assumes that the stones resist no pulling, never slide and never crush.",
          "start": 8.675,
          "end": 15.275
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Under those assumptions and a given load, the arch can stand if that line can stay inside the masonry.",
          "start": 15.675,
          "end": 23.05
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "If no such line fits, this idealized arch collapses.",
          "start": 23.45,
          "end": 28.05
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B41",
      "duration": 32.925,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B41.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "5065654bb29b281272e2018ff53ea0dbfb6f9272b9cc2ce697381ff3e04b4a73",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "That puts shape and proportion at the center of the question.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 4.0
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Unlike some other engineering problems, stability can be scaled, so a small model with the same proportions helps show what proportion does.",
          "start": 4.4,
          "end": 14.5
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "On its own, that does not show a whole real building is safe: this kind of analysis can miss effects such as local crushing, cracking and sliding.",
          "start": 14.9,
          "end": 25.05
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "But it helps explain how rules of geometry, learned by trial and error, could carry builders so far.",
          "start": 25.45,
          "end": 32.925
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B42",
      "duration": 19.525,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B42.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "eb76f58867fd0254d1d91245685dd77a1c15fb357e074045a64598321f35d261",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "So the heights were never impossible.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.875
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Pointed arches gave builders taller, more adaptable shapes, ribs helped direct the load toward the piers, and flying buttresses carried the thrust outside and down to the ground.",
          "start": 3.275,
          "end": 15.7
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "The walls in between could open up to glass.",
          "start": 16.1,
          "end": 19.525
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B43",
      "duration": 19.85,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B43.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "2be9c43c1346cd5d81fb45f836f6e4f6e3588b45eab2c02deb34aebf6a851d2a",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "But it is not a simple story of progress.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.25
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Beauvais needed new piers, Amiens needed an iron chain, and Suger's bright choir rose above a crypt of older forms.",
          "start": 3.65,
          "end": 12.4
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "Each cathedral was a test in stone, built by people who learned from centuries of trial and error.",
          "start": 12.8,
          "end": 19.85
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B44",
      "duration": 8.35,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B44.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "e596ab7f2a604b95a1f1efe386b808aa8fd1623248b092e80bd18e30f3286327",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "These models are illustrations, not structural analyses, and the arrows show ideas, not calculated forces.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 8.35
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B45",
      "duration": 11.45,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B45.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "813be520d1b1ff90f806c110ca97ddc21616c24eaaa6295767c1bb987412815e",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Which building or structure should we explain next?",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.525
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "Suggest a topic in the comments.",
          "start": 3.925,
          "end": 6.75
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "And if you enjoyed this film, please like it and subscribe.",
          "start": 7.15,
          "end": 11.45
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B46",
      "duration": 6.2,
      "audio_file": "audio/beats/B46.wav",
      "audio_sha256": "f43ee35e391fcbbbd1ccd315689d6be590b748096f94b8f572d78984198b2142",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "text": "Thank you very much for watching.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.575
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "The sources are listed in the description.",
          "start": 2.975,
          "end": 6.2
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
